  "statement": "Find $\\displaystyle\\int \\frac{e^x}{1+e^{2x}}\\,dx$.",
  "solution": "Let $u=e^x$, so $du=e^x\\,dx$. Then\n$$\\int\\frac{e^x}{1+e^{2x}}\\,dx=\\int\\frac{1}{1+u^2}\\,du=\\arctan u+C=\\arctan(e^x)+C.$$",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
